    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0532" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/26975: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vera Cruz</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-02-09T15:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                                1924—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Puerto Mexico has been evacuated by the De la Huerta forces. I have just been
                    informed that the De la Huerta forces will leave this city today and that the
                    Federal troops will reach here by tomorrow.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d350-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d350-f1" n="16" xml:id="d350-f1-content">
                <p>The consul reported on Feb. 11 that the Federal forces had arrived and on Feb. 17
                    that the <hi rendition="#italic">Richmond</hi> had left.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
